course: dictionary
lesson: 7386
title: Plumbing: pipes, jobs and clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Plumbing» is a noun, and it is also the -ing form of the verb «plumb». It means the system of pipes, taps, toilets and drains that bring clean water into a building and take dirty water away.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Indoor plumbing» means pipes inside the house, and «the plumbing is blocked» tells you water cannot get through. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? If your meaning of pipes and drains makes sense in the sentence, you have it.
explain: The word can also mean a job. «Fix the plumbing» means someone, a plumber, must put in or repair the pipes. So check the words around it to see whether the sentence is about the pipes themselves or the work done on them.
explain: Plants have plumbing too, in a way. «A plant is built like a house with plumbing: the stem is a bundle of pipes and a pillar.» Here the author compares a plant to a house, so plumbing is a picture of how water moves inside the stem.
fact: Plumbing means the pipes, taps, toilets and drains in a building.
fact: «Plumbing» can also mean the job of putting in and fixing pipes, which is done by a plumber.
fact: «Plumbing» comes from the Latin word «plumbum», which means lead, because the Romans had lead pipes.
fact: Clean water and good drains stop disease, which is why plumbing matters in science and history.
fact: As a joking, informal word, someone's plumbing can mean the inside of their body, such as the bladder or bowels.
exercise: «The plumbing is blocked, so the sink will not drain.» What is blocked? | *The pipes and drains | The roof | The toilet lid | The taps only
exercise: A plumber is coming to «fix the plumbing». What is the plumber's job? | Growing plants in the garden | Cooking the dinner | *Putting in and fixing pipes | Painting the walls
exercise: Which word comes from the Latin «plumbum», meaning lead? | Pillar | *Plumbing | Drain | Stem
test: In «A plant is built like a house with plumbing», what does plumbing mean? | Roots that dig deep into the soil | Seeds that fall to the ground | Leaves that catch the sunlight | *The pipes that carry water through the plant, like pipes in a house
test: Why does plumbing matter in science and history? | It makes rivers flow faster | *It stops disease by bringing clean water in and taking dirty water away | It lets people fly | It makes buildings taller
exam: Which sentence uses plumbing to mean a job? | «The plumbing is blocked» means water cannot get through | *«He is training in plumbing to become a plumber» | «Indoor plumbing» means pipes inside the house | «A plant is built like a house with plumbing»
